-- title:
--   The filtering host over an oracle of time n^2.9955609 runs in time O(n^2.99556095)
-- statement:
--   Let $T_o$ be such that for all real $c,\kappa$, eventually for every $U\le cn^{\kappa}$ and every $p\le$ `PmaxOf n`, $T_o(n,U,s(n),p)\le n^{2.9955609}$, where $s(n)=$ `Light.Filter2.sOf n`. Then for all real $c,\kappa$ there is $K$ such that eventually, for every $U\le cn^{\kappa}$, $\mathrm{filterTime}(T_o,n,U)\le K\,n^{2.99556095}$.
--
--   `filterTime` is the time of the filtering host: parameters, prime sieve, marks, `roundsOf n` rounds of `rOf n` steps with one oracle call per pool prime, and the final answer.
-- source:
--   Developed for the prove2.me APSP exponent campaign (https://prove2.me/campaigns/apsp-exponent) on top of the Lean formalization anthropics/formal-math, folder 3sum-apsp, commit e1a4e65 (https://github.com/anthropics/formal-math/tree/e1a4e6508154ea59f030480661590a9fe3018011/3sum-apsp; Lean v4.33.1, Mathlib v4.33.1). The statement comes from the file 3sum-apsp/ThreeSumApsp/Filter2/Final.lean of the campaign's modified copy of that library, which is not published; the new definitions it uses are in the platform definition bundles APSP2995561_Defs1 and APSP2995561_Defs2 (and APSP2996001_Defs1-2, APSP299791_Defs1-5 of the earlier entries). It follows the technical note "Deterministic APSP via thin products" (revised 7 October 2026) refining J. Alman and V. Vassilevska Williams, "Truly Subquadratic 3SUM and Truly Subcubic APSP via Triangles in Sparse Lopsided Graphs", arXiv:2610.06783v1 (https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.06783v1), Lemma 3.1 and Section 3.

